/* ==========================================================================
 *  dt_sample.js -- a real recording of a live DTaaS stack, bundled so the
 *  standalone page self-demos with nothing running.
 *
 *  Captured from an ORBIT broker hosting the `dt` plugin plus two rhapsody
 *  endpoints ('viz_task_ep' for the twins' components and their in-situ
 *  inference, 'viz_exsitu_ep' for the ROSE learner's tasks).  Sixty-one
 *  seconds, 1 Hz `admin/sessions` polls interleaved with the gateway's SSE
 *  notifications, holding three twins:
 *
 *    - a `CalibrationLearner` (test/10-learner) that refits a sensor
 *      calibration ex-situ while serving predictions in-situ -- the `rmse`
 *      criterion crosses its 0.25 target and keeps hovering around it;
 *    - an in-situ twin (counting sensor + offset model) created at t=10 s
 *      and closed at t=34 s -- the create and destroy arcs;
 *    - a twin whose persistent component raises -- `failed`, with the
 *      reason in `last_error`.
 *
 *  A .js file rather than a .json one for exactly one reason: a classic
 *  <script src> loads from `file://`, and `fetch()` does not -- this is
 *  what lets the page work offline with no server at all.  The content is
 *  the recording schema documented in dt_dash.js, verbatim; the timestamps
 *  are rounded to 10 ms to keep the file small.
 * ========================================================================*/

